A stronger exact control variate is possible from the first layer’s full second moment: for any random projection `r`, `E[(h1 @ r)^2]` is known exactly from the first-layer Gaussian kernel. I’m testing random quadratic features plus regression to see whether they reduce final residuals enough to justify their extra FLOPs.
