codex
A more promising variance reduction is at the last layer: sample the actual final preactivations, estimate their mean/variance, then use the Gaussian ReLU moment formula instead of the noisy post-ReLU sample mean. I’m testing that plug-in Rao-Blackwell-style final row on synthetic MLPs.
